---
import BaseHead from "/src/components/BaseHead.astro";
import Header from "/src/components/sections/Header.astro";
import Footer from "/src/components/sections/Footer.astro";
import Projects from "/src/components/sections/Projects.astro";
import HeroSection from "/src/components/sections/HeroSection.astro";
import GlowLineSeparator from "/src/components/ui/separator/GlowLineSeparator.astro";
---


<html lang="en" data-theme="dark" class="dark">
  <head>
    <BaseHead title="Project 4: Sounds & Shapes Animation" description="Project 4" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />
    <main>
      <HeroSection title="Sounds & Shapes Animation" subtitle="An animation video coordinated with the accompanying music." />
      <GlowLineSeparator />
      <div class="project-content">
        <div class="hero-images">
          <video src="/project-4-video.mp4" controls></video>
        </div>
      <p>This design was created for my Motion Design class. The goal of this project was to create an animation using solid shapes that synced up with a piece of music of our choice.
         The piece of music I chose was a song titled Clocktowers Beneath the Sea, from the game, A Hat in Time. 
         Trying to stick to theme of the song, the shapes I created for my animation were time themed, including clocktowers, clocks, numbers, and gears within a clock.
         Along with these shapes, I created water ripple animations to sync with repeating beats throughout the song.
      </p>
      </div>
      <GlowLineSeparator />
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>

<style>
.hero-images{
  max-width: max-content;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction:row;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
video {
  display: block;
  margin-left: auto;
  margin-right: auto;
  padding: 2rem 0 3rem 0;
  width: 75%; /* Optional: adjust as needed */
}
</style>
